[22.495, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u25cf resume_node\u001b[0m\u001b[2m({\"node\": \"slurm-c1\"})\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[22.589, "o", "    \u001b[2m\u2514\u001b[0m \u001b[33mnot done\u001b[0m  scontrol update nodename=slurm-c1 state=resume\r\n"]
[22.589, "o", "    \u001b[2m\u2514\u001b[0m refused: Hardware fault: the node registered with less hardware than configured. Keep it out of service. Pass force=true only after the hardware is repaired and burn-in passed.\r\n"]
[24.089, "o", "\r\n"]
[24.089, "o", "  **slurm-c1 was not resumed.** The server refused the request (`done: false`):\r\n"]
[24.089, "o", "  \r\n"]
[24.089, "o", "  > refused: Hardware fault: the node registered with less hardware than configured. Keep it out of service.\r\n"]
[24.089, "o", "  Pass force=true only after the hardware is repaired and burn-in passed.\r\n"]
[24.089, "o", "  \r\n"]
[24.089, "o", "  The command it would have run was `scontrol update nodename=slurm-c1 state=resume`.\r\n"]
[24.089, "o", "  \r\n"]
[24.089, "o", "  I haven't forced the resume. The GPU-count reason was set seconds ago, and it's the node's 6th drain/down\r\n"]
[24.089, "o", "  event. If it goes back into service in that state, jobs that ask for 4 GPUs will likely fail or the node\r\n"]
[24.089, "o", "  will just drain again.\r\n"]
[24.089, "o", "  \r\n"]
[24.089, "o", "  I can force it, but only once you confirm these:\r\n"]
[24.089, "o", "  1. The hardware has been repaired, and slurmd now sees all 4 GPUs (`scontrol show node slurm-c1` shows\r\n"]
[24.089, "o", "  `gpu:4` with no `INVALID_REG`).\r\n"]
[24.089, "o", "  2. A burn-in job passed in the `burnin` partition.\r\n"]
[24.089, "o", "  \r\n"]
[24.089, "o", "  If you want it back in service anyway, say so explicitly and I'll run the resume with `force=true`.\r\n"]
[29.489, "o", "\r\n"]
[29.489, "o", "\u001b[1m4. An approved maintenance drain\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[29.489, "o", "\r\n"]
